WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.164
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online C two, Book two.

2
00:00:05.464 --> 00:00:08.711
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.011 --> 00:00:15.646
Unit nine: Consciousness Studies. Today you will explain the mind using nominalized abstract concepts.

4
00:00:15.946 --> 00:00:18.633
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.567 --> 00:00:22.683
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.550 --> 00:00:24.714
Consciousness.

7
00:00:25.717 --> 00:00:29.806
Consciousness means the state of being aware of oneself and one's surroundings.

8
00:00:30.417 --> 00:00:33.647
Consciousness remains the least understood feature of the brain.

9
00:00:34.250 --> 00:00:37.274
Your turn. Say: Consciousness.

10
00:00:40.133 --> 00:00:41.320
Consciousness.

11
00:00:42.083 --> 00:00:42.899
Qualia.

12
00:00:43.883 --> 00:00:48.542
Qualia means the private, felt quality of an experience, such as the redness of red.

13
00:00:49.150 --> 00:00:52.659
No equation seems to capture the qualia of tasting mango.

14
00:00:53.250 --> 00:00:55.589
Your turn. Say: Qualia.

15
00:00:58.433 --> 00:00:59.225
Qualia.

16
00:00:59.983 --> 00:01:01.693
Subjective experience.

17
00:01:02.683 --> 00:01:07.086
Subjective experience means what something feels like from the inside to one person.

18
00:01:07.683 --> 00:01:11.273
Subjective experience cannot be directly observed by others.

19
00:01:11.883 --> 00:01:15.209
Your turn. Say: Subjective experience.

20
00:01:18.067 --> 00:01:19.939
Subjective experience.

21
00:01:20.683 --> 00:01:21.719
Hard problem.

22
00:01:22.717 --> 00:01:27.363
Hard problem means the puzzle of why physical processes give rise to felt experience.

23
00:01:27.950 --> 00:01:30.971
Chalmers named it the hard problem of consciousness.

24
00:01:31.583 --> 00:01:34.607
Your turn. Say: Hard problem.

25
00:01:37.467 --> 00:01:39.373
Hard problem.

26
00:01:40.117 --> 00:01:41.396
Awareness.

27
00:01:42.383 --> 00:01:46.322
Awareness means knowledge or perception of a situation or fact.

28
00:01:46.917 --> 00:01:51.029
Awareness of one's own thoughts distinguishes reflection from reflex.

29
00:01:51.617 --> 00:01:53.967
Your turn. Say: Awareness.

30
00:01:56.833 --> 00:01:58.020
Awareness.

31
00:01:58.783 --> 00:01:59.773
Perception.

32
00:02:00.783 --> 00:02:04.559
Perception means the way something is sensed and interpreted by the mind.

33
00:02:05.150 --> 00:02:08.891
Perception is an active construction, not a passive recording.

34
00:02:09.483 --> 00:02:11.996
Your turn. Say: Perception.

35
00:02:14.833 --> 00:02:15.800
Perception.

36
00:02:16.550 --> 00:02:17.714
Sentience.

37
00:02:18.717 --> 00:02:21.645
Sentience means the capacity to feel and perceive.

38
00:02:22.250 --> 00:02:25.840
Debates about animal sentience shape laws on welfare.

39
00:02:26.450 --> 00:02:28.951
Your turn. Say: Sentience.

40
00:02:31.800 --> 00:02:32.848
Sentience.

41
00:02:33.583 --> 00:02:34.863
Introspection.

42
00:02:35.850 --> 00:02:39.382
Introspection means examining one's own thoughts and feelings.

43
00:02:39.983 --> 00:02:43.655
Introspection is useful, yet notoriously unreliable.

44
00:02:44.250 --> 00:02:46.809
Your turn. Say: Introspection.

45
00:02:49.667 --> 00:02:50.958
Introspection.

46
00:02:51.767 --> 00:02:55.208
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:56.050 --> 00:03:00.839
Visal, scientists can map the brain in detail. Hasn't consciousness been explained?

48
00:03:01.950 --> 00:03:10.164
Not at all. The hard problem concerns the nature of subjective experience, which no brain scan directly reveals.

49
00:03:11.250 --> 00:03:14.016
But activity in the brain correlates with feelings.

50
00:03:15.117 --> 00:03:23.028
Correlation is not explanation. The emergence of qualia from neurons remains a mystery, however detailed the measurement.

51
00:03:24.117 --> 00:03:26.116
So science has reached a limit?

52
00:03:27.217 --> 00:03:36.522
Perhaps only a pause. The recognition of that gap is itself progress, and it calls for humility on every side.

53
00:03:37.667 --> 00:03:39.097
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:39.950 --> 00:03:43.761
Grammar focus: Nominalized abstract concepts.

55
00:03:44.061 --> 00:03:45.294
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:45.983 --> 00:03:49.631
The hard problem concerns the nature of subjective experience.

57
00:03:50.517 --> 00:03:53.770
The emergence of qualia remains a scientific mystery.

58
00:03:54.683 --> 00:03:57.995
The recognition of that gap demands intellectual humility.

59
00:03:58.933 --> 00:04:10.978
Turn processes into nouns (recognise → recognition, emerge → emergence) and let them act as subjects. The result is dense and academic: abstract noun + verb + abstract noun.

60
00:04:11.717 --> 00:04:15.739
Be careful! Don't say: Consciousness is hardly to explain.

61
00:04:17.700 --> 00:04:20.988
Say: The explanation of consciousness is hard.

62
00:04:21.288 --> 00:04:24.588
Nominalise: explain → explanation.

63
00:04:25.400 --> 00:04:27.959
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:04:28.767 --> 00:04:29.988
The Hard Problem.

65
00:04:30.288 --> 00:04:35.782
Neuroscience can now trace which regions of the brain activate when a person sees, remembers or decides.

66
00:04:36.767 --> 00:04:46.603
Yet the philosopher David Chalmers argued that an explanation of function leaves untouched a deeper question: why any of this processing should be accompanied by subjective experience.

67
00:04:47.600 --> 00:04:54.174
That felt quality, which philosophers call qualia, appears resistant to description in physical terms alone.

68
00:04:55.167 --> 00:05:02.008
Some thinkers therefore doubt that introspection can be trusted, while others maintain that sentience may extend well beyond humans.

69
00:05:03.000 --> 00:05:09.818
The honest conclusion is that consciousness remains unexplained, and that humility is more productive than premature certainty.

70
00:05:10.933 --> 00:05:15.179
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:05:16.017 --> 00:05:19.282
The hard problem blank the nature of subjective experience.

72
00:05:19.582 --> 00:05:23.595
A, concerns. B, concerned to. C, concerning.

73
00:05:27.133 --> 00:05:29.307
The answer is A: concerns.

74
00:05:30.450 --> 00:05:33.541
The private felt quality of an experience is blank.

75
00:05:33.841 --> 00:05:37.599
A, qualia. B, perception. C, introspection.

76
00:05:41.133 --> 00:05:43.168
The answer is A: qualia.

77
00:05:44.317 --> 00:05:46.885
The capacity to feel and perceive is blank.

78
00:05:47.185 --> 00:05:51.837
A, sentience. B, awareness only. C, essence.

79
00:05:55.400 --> 00:05:57.400
The answer is A: sentience.

80
00:05:58.550 --> 00:06:00.433
Which uses a nominalization?

81
00:06:00.733 --> 00:06:09.019
A, Neurons fire and we feel.. B, The emergence of feeling puzzles scientists.. C, We puzzle about why feelings emerge..

82
00:06:12.567 --> 00:06:16.830
The answer is B: The emergence of feeling puzzles scientists..

83
00:06:17.983 --> 00:06:21.655
According to the reading, the honest conclusion is that consciousness…

84
00:06:21.955 --> 00:06:27.895
A, has been fully explained. B, remains unexplained. C, is an illusion.

85
00:06:31.433 --> 00:06:33.828
The answer is B: remains unexplained.

86
00:06:35.033 --> 00:06:38.382
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:06:39.217 --> 00:06:42.400
Why do some philosophers call consciousness the 'hard problem'?

88
00:06:59.217 --> 00:07:00.659
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:07:00.959 --> 00:07:32.180
Some philosophers call consciousness the hard problem because explaining brain function does not explain why there is felt experience at all. We can describe how the brain processes light, but not why seeing red feels like something. That private quality, qualia, seems resistant to physical description. The gap is not a failure of effort; it may be a gap in our concepts. I think humility is the right response.

90
00:07:32.480 --> 00:07:34.305
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:07:35.217 --> 00:07:40.028
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and nominalized abstract concepts.

92
00:07:40.328 --> 00:07:46.092
Today's value is intellectual humility. Admit what you do not know, and stay ready to learn.

93
00:07:46.392 --> 00:07:48.743
See you in Unit ten. Goodbye!

94
00:07:49.043 --> 00:07:53.692
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

